<title>JAPAN: Japan Mar tin imports up 46.4 pct year/year--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Mar tin imports up 46.4 pct year/year--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan imported 2,470 tonnes of refined tin in March, up 46.4 percent from 1,687 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry data said on Monday.</p>
<p>The imports (on a customs-cleared basis in tonnes) were as follows:</p>
<p>			Mar 97     Feb 97	  Mar 96</p>
<p> Total		2,470	2,274	   1,687</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Indonesia	    860	  980	     699</p>
<p> Malaysia	     795	  402	     399</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first three months of 1997 were 6,911 tonnes, slightly up from 6,046 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 6179</p>
</text>
